&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Experience&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–6 years of experience in partner marketing, co-marketing, marketing operations, or program/project coordination — ideally in a tech, gaming, or platform company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting cross-functional marketing programs, from intake through launch and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some experience working directly with external partners or clients in a marketing capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Skills&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid project management instincts: comfortable tracking timelines, managing dependencies across multiple stakeholders, and flagging risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communicator, able to organize information clearly for review by others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented and organized, with the ability to manage an asset tracker or partner approval request end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in fast-paced environments with shifting priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good analytical instincts — comfortable pulling data and connecting program activity to business metrics with guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Tools&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in project management and workflow tools (e.g., Asana, Salesforce, Notion, Google Workspace, Claude / AI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cross-functional marketing operations, including intake and approval workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with presentation-heavy environments (Google Slides / PowerPoint) — you&#39;ll frequently build and review partner-facing materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the gaming industry or with game developer partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in or exposure to developer marketing, platform marketing, or B2B marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with co-marketing in a deal context — where marketing is part of a larger commercial negotiation.&lt;/li&gt;
